{"Calling `parseRefreshTokenResponse` when credential sync is enabled in packages/app-store/office365calendar/lib/CalendarService.ts replaces the real OAuth `refresh_token` with the literal placeholder string `\"refresh_token\"`, which is then saved to the DB.": 0.9330715537071228, "`[z.string().toString()]` is a computed property that evaluates to a fixed literal string (like `\"ZodString\"`) in packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/parseRefreshTokenResponse.ts, not a dynamic key matcher. Use `.passthrough()` on the object schema instead.": 0.8662292957305908, "`parseRefreshTokenResponse` returns a Zod `safeParse` result (`{ success, data }`) in packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts, not the parsed value directly. Storing this as `key` corrupts the credential in the database. Access `.data` to get the actual credential object.": 0.9877790808677673, "The raw `fetch` `Response` is returned without parsing in packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/refreshOAuthTokens.ts. Callers access properties like `.data`, `.expiresIn`, `.expiryDate` on the return value, which don't exist on a `Response` object. The response needs to be parsed with `await response.json()` before returning.": 0.9829015731811523, "When credential sharing is enabled in packages/app-store/googlecalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts, `refreshOAuthTokens` returns a native `fetch` `Response` (no `.data` property), but the next line accesses `res?.data` expecting a GaxiosResponse shape. This will cause a TypeError.": 0.9716833233833313, "`prisma` is used but never imported in packages/app-store/salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts. This will throw `ReferenceError: prisma is not defined` at runtime. Add `import prisma from \"@calcom/prisma\";` to the imports.": 0.9645639061927795, "`credentialId` (the credential's database primary key) is passed as the `userId` parameter of `refreshOAuthTokens` in packages/app-store/zoho-bigin/lib/CalendarService.ts, which forwards it to the sync endpoint as `calcomUserId`. This sends the wrong identifier to the credential sync service. The user's actual ID (`credential.userId`) should be passed instead.": 0.9982959628105164, "Missing `!!` coercion in packages/lib/constants.ts: `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED` evaluates to the literal `CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY` string (a secret) instead of a boolean. If this constant is ever logged or serialized, the encryption key leaks.": 0.928827166557312, "Webhook secret comparison in apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts is vulnerable to timing attacks. Use `crypto.timingSafeEqual` for constant-time string comparison.": 0.713890790939331, "The parser call in packages/app-store/zoomvideo/lib/VideoApiAdapter.ts can return token data that does not match `zoomRefreshedTokenSchema` in credential-sharing mode, but the code still persists `refresh_token`/`expires_in` as if they were guaranteed.": 0.6784592866897583, "The slug is hardcoded in packages/app-store/zoho-bigin/api/add.ts instead of using the already-imported `appConfig.slug`, creating an inconsistency with `callback.ts` in the same directory.": 0.38534098863601685, "The `!parsedToken.success` check in packages/app-store/zoomvideo/lib/VideoApiAdapter.ts is now dead code since `parseRefreshTokenResponse` already throws an error internally when parsing fails.": 0.26413583755493164, "The check `if (!accessTokenParsed.success)` in packages/app-store/salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts is unreachable since `parseRefreshTokenResponse` throws an error internally when parsing fails.": 0.306615948677063, "`response.statusText` is unreliable in packages/app-store/salesforce/lib/CalendarService.ts\u2014HTTP/2 omits it and some Node.js fetch implementations return an empty string. Use `!response.ok` instead.": 0.6775545477867126, "No error handling for the fetch response in packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/refreshOAuthTokens.ts. If `CALCOM_CREDENTIAL_SYNC_ENDPOINT` returns a non-2xx status, the error is silently swallowed.": 0.9557639956474304, "Webhook handler in apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts does not validate HTTP method. Should restrict to POST to prevent accidental triggers from GET requests.": 0.7971172332763672, "`refreshOAuthTokens` can return the credential-sync response (which doesn't include Lark's `code`/`msg` fields) in packages/app-store/larkcalendar/lib/CalendarService.ts. `handleLarkError` will treat that as an error and throw.": 0.6326001882553101, "Neither `symmetricDecrypt` nor `JSON.parse` is wrapped in error handling in apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts. If the encrypted payload is corrupted, this will throw an unhandled exception.": 0.9521957039833069, "The missing encryption key is silently replaced with a hardcoded empty string `\"\"` in apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts. Throw an explicit error instead of falling back to a useless default for a cryptographic secret.": 0.8348590135574341, "When credential syncing is enabled in packages/app-store/webex/lib/VideoApiAdapter.ts, refreshOAuthTokens returns a payload that contains only access_token/expiry_date, but this adapter still validates against the full Webex refresh schema.": 0.6597157716751099, "refreshOAuthTokens can return the credential-sync response in packages/app-store/office365video/lib/VideoApiAdapter.ts, but this path still treats it like a Microsoft refresh response, causing the credential to become immediately expired.": 0.7817436456680298, "Unnecessarily roundabout import path in packages/app-store/_utils/oauth/createOAuthAppCredential.ts. Since this file is already inside `_utils/oauth/`, importing `../oauth/decodeOAuthState` navigates up then back down. The original `./decodeOAuthState` was simpler.": 0.6191040873527527, "`CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is out of alphabetical order in turbo.json \u2014 it should appear before `CALENDSO_ENCRYPTION_KEY`.": 0.16593396663665771}